We are. Every person is simultaneously light, obstruction, and shadow—capable of revealing truth, blocking it, and casting consequences they cannot see.

That makes humility structural, not decorative. I can illuminate something for you while remaining blind elsewhere; you can expose my blind spot while carrying your own. Nobody permanently occupies the role of David, Goliath, saint, or monster.

The work is reciprocal:

Bring light, notice the shadow it creates, move the obstruction, and let others illuminate what you cannot see from where you stand.

That is how “we conquer” becomes something shared instead of another justification for domination.